# Shade timing tests, 2026-11-15 (clone only, no original remote unless noted)
#
# Firmware v0.9.1 to v0.9.3 (bring-up firmware, src/main.cpp). One group-4
# shade, switch A. Clone ID C1 0E (made up; not a real remote's ID).
# IR: TSAL6200 on a long extension lead, taped to the shade beside its sensor
# eye with the LED's tip pointing up (side light only). The tape failed once;
# the runs it spoiled are left out (see the notes). Lines are copied from the
# serial monitor; timestamps are the PC's. "# ..." lines are the tester's notes.
#
# Convention in runs without notes: a repeated command means the one before it
# failed (the tester repeated until the shade responded).
#
# seq step = RF wake ID 01 00 80 on one channel (ch 33, 52, 71 in turn) for
# `seq rf` ms, then IR for `seq ir` ms. Defaults from v0.9.1: rf 50, gap 0, ir 50.

## 1. Baseline: arrow keys (seq, 3 steps, ~317 ms per press), ~1-1.5 s apart
# 12 of 13; the only miss was the first press.

13:59:54.790 > Seq 0110:  RF ch33 x183 @0 ms, IR @51 ms;  RF ch52 x185 @103 ms, IR @154 ms;  RF ch71 x181 @205 ms, IR @256 ms  (total 318 ms)
13:59:56.237 > Seq 0110:  RF ch33 x184 @0 ms, IR @51 ms;  RF ch52 x182 @102 ms, IR @153 ms;  RF ch71 x183 @204 ms, IR @255 ms  (total 317 ms)
13:59:58.318 > Seq 0101:  RF ch33 x183 @0 ms, IR @51 ms;  RF ch52 x181 @102 ms, IR @153 ms;  RF ch71 x182 @204 ms, IR @255 ms  (total 317 ms)
# ... 10 more presses alternating UP / DOWN, all worked.

